From a451d49bce347477169cd0ca8d69a6114def7f93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:38:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Per-rank snapshots of the loaded weights
 (VLLM_EXL3_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT=1)

Loading MiniMax-M3.1 EXL3 at TP=2 spends ~120-150 s per rank in per-tensor
Python (~90,000 tensors), not in bytes. With VLLM_EXL3_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT=1 the
first boot of a configuration writes every CUDA storage behind the model's
parameters and buffers (plus tensors the load parks in module attributes,
such as the MiniMax indexer payloads) to one O_DIRECT file per rank with a
CRC32 per 64 MiB chunk; later boots plan the trellis arenas the way the
loader does, require an identical layout, read the storages back and replay
the plain attributes, then run process_weights_after_loading as usual.

Fail-closed: a missing, stale or mismatched snapshot loads the checkpoint, a
CRC failure deletes the snapshot and loads the checkpoint, and a load with
side effects that cannot be replayed writes no snapshot. The key covers the
checkpoint files, the serve config, the plugin sources, torch/vLLM/exllamav3,
every VLLM_EXL3_*/EXL3_* variable, the TP rank and size, the device and
VLLM_EXL3_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT_TAG. The idea follows the processed-weight snapshots
of kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 and the author's earlier DGX Spark recipe;
no code is shared.
---
 src/vllm_exl3/__init__.py        |   6 +
 src/vllm_exl3/weight_snapshot.py | 677 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 683 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/vllm_exl3/weight_snapshot.py

